Q4 — Longest Palindromic Substring
A palindrome is a string that reads the same forwards and backwards.
Given a string s, find the longest continuous substring of s that is a palindrome.
If multiple palindromic substrings have the same maximum length, return any one of them.



def long_pali(string):
    longest = ""
    for i in range(len(string)):
        for j in range(i+1,len(string)+1):
            temp = string[i:j]
            if temp==temp[::-1] and len(temp)>len(longest):
                longest = temp
    return longest

string = "cbbd"
print(long_pali(string))
